  "truth_boundary": "The canonical path withholds every event version and Evidence unless the entire strict seven-day batch passes, rejects future timestamps beyond 300 seconds, requires a separately supplied exact registry digest, disables raw full-bundle persistence, and emits only a redacted private candidate receipt from realpath-contained 0700/0600 storage. The standalone runner cannot self-assert governed receipt authority or lawful empirical admission. Atomic Governed Landing uses the repository GITHUB_TOKEN, so its merge-generated push cannot be treated as authoritative post-merge workflow evidence. V1.3 stages a trusted validator before the merge, globally serializes landing on protected main, then checks out the exact server-returned merge SHA in the same trusted job, verifies both merge parents and the Current-SOLD change surface, reruns 56 tests and all no-write guards, and publishes an exact-merge status without adding a workflow_run consumer, credentials, writes, provider calls, deployment, or release authority."
